= Petit FatFs

This is a copy of Petit FatFs, a FAT file system module for systems with very
tight code space or working memory, by ChaN.
See https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/00index_p.html.

Please submit upstream bug reports to the
https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/bd/[FatFs User Forum], not to this repo.

== Releases

Each official release archive is imported in a separate commit and tagged with
its upstream version: R0.01a, R0.02, R0.02a, R0.03 and R0.03a. Commit messages
record the archive URL and SHA-256. Older `src` and `doc` directories are named
`source` and `documents`; their file contents are preserved.

This repository is Petit-only. The mixed https://github.com/pabigot/FatFs[release
mirror] was used as a provenance reference, not as the source of this history.
Some archives have been repackaged since that mirror's imports, so historical
ZIP checksums can differ; the current official archive checksum is recorded.

The repository README is added after the first upstream import and retained in
subsequent releases. Documentation and pristine upstream imports do not create
XMOS releases. Reserve `<upstream-version>+xmos.<N>` tags for actual downstream
source patches. XMOS build configuration and storage adapters belong in the
consuming library.

The https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/pfpatches.html[known-problems page] describes a
May 2021 R0.03a patch for CP857 and FAT32-disabled builds. Its advertised patch
download returned HTTP 404 when this history was prepared. That patch has not
been applied; do not describe this checkout as including it.

